## Core Service Offerings

### RF PCB Design and Layout
**Headline:** RF PCB layout validated in real-world conditions, not just simulations.

- Standards & Interfaces: ISM, Wi-Fi, BLE, LTE, Sub-GHz, 5G NR, 77 GHz mmWave.
- Tools: HFSS, controlled-impedance layout, Smith Chart matching, VSWR < 1.5:1.
- Substrates: Rogers 4350B/3003, Panasonic Megtron 6, Tachyon 100G for high-frequency paths.

### RF Front-End (RFFE) Design
**Headline:** RF front-end architecture, LNA, PA, filters, and matching networks.

- LNA and PA design for 4G LTE, 5G NR sub-6 GHz and mmWave.
- SAW/BAW filtering, carrier aggregation, beamforming architectures.
- WiFi 6/6E/7: 4x4 and 8x8 MU-MIMO, 320 MHz channels, OFDMA, Multi-Link Operation (MLO).
- LPWAN: LoRaWAN, Sigfox, BLE 5.4 — sleep-current profiling, antenna feed matching.

### Simulation and Modeling
**Headline:** Pre-layout full-wave simulation to predict real-world RF behavior.

- 3D EM simulation: HFSS for trace geometry, matching networks, and antenna structures.
- Smith Chart-based matching, S-parameter analysis, EVM measurement.
- Pre-compliance EMI/EMC scans before formal FCC Part 15 / CE testing.

---

## Technical Advantage

- **Signal Integrity (SI)** — Engineers mitigate skin-effect losses, copper-roughness impact, and via-stub resonance at frequencies exceeding 24 GHz.
- **Noise Floor Reduction** — Analog, digital, power, and RF domains are partitioned to prevent cross-talk and receiver desensitization.
- **RF Generators** — High-power RF generators — 1 kW HF and 500W LF — for plasma etching, thin-film deposition, and medical ablation at 13.56 MHz ISM.
- **WiFi 6/6E and WiFi 7** — High-Efficiency (HE) and Extremely High Throughput (EHT), with 4x4/8x8 MU-MIMO and OFDMA sub-carrier mapping.
- **Cellular (4G LTE / 5G NR)** — RFFE with LNA and PA, carrier aggregation, beamforming for sub-6 GHz and mmWave.
- **LPWAN and Short Range** — LoRaWAN, Sigfox, BLE 5.4 optimized for ultra-low power and maximum battery life.
- **Industrial Sensing** — Microwave-based NDT sensors for moisture measurement and material-density analysis using phase-shift detection.
- **Substrate Selection** — Rogers 4350B/3003, Megtron 6, Tachyon 100G; surface-finish selection and skin-effect analysis.
- **EMI/EMC Pre-compliance** — Early-stage simulation and internal testing for RE and CE; ground-loop elimination and common-mode choke selection.
- **Power Electronics Integration** — Thermal dissipation and EMI shielding in high-density power RF modules.
- **Impedance Matching** — Smith Charts for complex conjugate matching, VSWR < 1.5:1.
- **Precision Layout** — Controlled-impedance traces with phase matching and propagation-delay requirements.

