## FAQ

**Q: What frequency ranges do Qmax Systems RF services cover?**
A: Qmax Systems covers LF and HF through mmWave (24 GHz to 77 GHz+). This spans sub-GHz LPWAN, 2.4/5/6 GHz WiFi, sub-6 GHz 5G NR, and 77 GHz automotive radar.

**Q: Can Qmax Systems assist with WiFi 6/6E and WiFi 7 transitions?**
A: Yes. Qmax Systems designs WiFi 6, 6E, and WiFi 7 hardware including 4x4/8x8 MU-MIMO, concurrent tri-band (2.4/5/6 GHz), 320 MHz channels, 4096-QAM, and Multi-Link Operation (MLO) on current Qualcomm and MediaTek SoCs.

**Q: How does Qmax Systems handle EMI/EMC issues in compact designs?**
A: Qmax Systems uses board-level shielding, analog/digital/RF domain partitioning, and multi-layer stackups with continuous ground planes. Pre-compliance scans with near-field probes locate emission hotspots early.

**Q: Does Qmax Systems provide antenna design and tuning services?**
A: Yes. Custom PCB antennas, chip and external antenna selection, and impedance matching using Smith Chart-based L, Pi, and T networks to hold VSWR below 1.5:1.

**Q: What tools does Qmax Systems use for RF simulation?**
A: Full-wave 3D EM solvers including HFSS, circuit/EDA tools for schematic capture, controlled-impedance layout, and link-budget analysis.

**Q: Can Qmax Systems help with 4G/5G private network hardware?**
A: Yes. RFFE design for 4G LTE and private 5G NR, sub-6 GHz and mmWave bands, carrier aggregation, beamforming, SAW/BAW filtering.

**Q: What is Qmax Systems' experience with high-power RF?**
A: 1 kW HF and 500W LF RF generators for plasma etching, thin-film deposition, and medical ablation at 13.56 MHz ISM, with automatic impedance matching and high-VSWR protection.

**Q: Does Qmax Systems support LoRa and other LPWAN protocols?**
A: Yes. LoRaWAN, Sigfox, and other LPWAN devices with urban link ranges of 2-5 km typical.

**Q: How does Qmax Systems ensure ground loop elimination?**
A: Star-grounding, controlled split planes, differential signaling between circuit domains, single-point connections between analog/digital/power/RF grounds.

**Q: What in-house testing capabilities does Qmax Systems have?**
A: Rohde & Schwarz CMW500, spectrum analyzers, vector network analyzers, and high-bandwidth oscilloscopes.

**Q: Can Qmax Systems optimize a design for low power consumption?**
A: Yes. Hardware and firmware co-design, sleep and active current profiling, duty cycle and RF output power tuning.

**Q: Does Qmax Systems handle mmWave sensor integration?**
A: Yes. 24 GHz to 77 GHz+ proximity, velocity, and presence detection on low-loss substrates such as Rogers 4350B.

**Q: What materials does Qmax Systems recommend for Microwave PCBs?**
A: Below 1 GHz: FR-4. Above 1 GHz: Rogers 4350B/3003, Megtron 6, Taconic, or Tachyon 100G for low dissipation factor.

**Q: Can Qmax Systems help with FCC/CE certification?**
A: Qmax Systems performs extensive in-house pre-compliance testing to help products pass FCC Part 15 and CE on the first attempt. Final certification is issued by an accredited test house.